  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\r\n\r\n1.\tI would like to ensure that the renderer does not ever render an `<input type=\"checkbox\">` as `checked` by default.\r\n1.\tI would like to demonstrate explicitly the intended check state for an `<input type=\"checkbox\">` in markup so that a checkbox cannot accidentally be determined to be erroneously (un)checked.\r\n\r\n### What solutions exist today?\r\n\r\n1.\tAbsence of the `checked` property:\r\n\r\n\t```HTML\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\" checked>\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\">\r\n\t```\r\n\r\n1.\tA comment: \r\n\r\n\t```HTML\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\" checked>\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\"> <!-- Deliberately unchecked. -->\r\n\t```\r\n\r\n### How would you solve it?\r\n\r\nInclusion of an `unchecked` property:\r\n\r\n1.\t```HTML\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\" unchecked>\r\n\t```\r\n1.\t```HTML\r\n\t<input type=\"checkbox\" state=\"unchecked\">\r\n\t```\r\n\r\n### Anything else?\r\n\r\nCitations:\r\n\r\n1.\t> https://github.com/mdn/content/blob/9c09b183a5ce844a75c2f22e909d03f71ca329fc/files/en-us/web/html/element/input/checkbox/index.md?plain=1#L41:~:text=If%20a%20checkbox%20is%20unchecked,value%20indicating%20an%20unchecked%20state\r\n1.\t> https://stackoverflow.com/revisions/32230974/1#:~:text=Unchecked%20is%20the%20default%20state%20of%20the%20checkbox%20so%20you%20dont%20need%20to%20add%20anything\r\n1.\t> https://stackoverflow.com/revisions/12700656/2#:~:text=%3Cinput%20type=%22checkbox%22%20checked%20/%3E",
